<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.6.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01687</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.6.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2085d7a9-26fb-40b8-97ef-dea0dc7a9e7f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="d56227b2-abf5-4831-b15d-b10b90ce5382" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 1 – 5, factor using perfect square trinomials.</para><para>\(9y^2 + 24y + 16\)
        </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4y\;\ – \;\ 3)^2\)</para><para>\((3y\;\  – \;\ 4)^2\)</para><para>\((3y + 4)^2\)</para><para>\((4y + 3)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \((3y + 4)^2\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="aac53607-e6ea-4a04-a690-25c4faa22395" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(16z^2 − 72z + 81\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((4z − 9)^2\)</para><para>\((9z − 4)^2\)</para><para>\((9z + 4)^2\)</para><para>\((4z + 9)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \((4z − 9)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ec8d93e9-326b-4330-8957-642002d6560d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(27p^2q + 90pq + 75q\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((27p + 5)^2\)</para><para>\(9q(p + 5)^2\)</para><para>\(3q(3p + 5)^2\)</para><para>\(3q(3p − 5)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(3q(3p + 5)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="3b77377a-4f5d-47a8-ab6c-606c0229d3dc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(64z^2 − 16z + 1\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((z − 8)^2\)</para><para>\((8z + 1)^2\)</para><para>\((z + 8)^2\)</para><para>\((8z − 1)^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \((8z − 1)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="9194da46-330c-4425-b48a-9ed09b715190" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(64x^2y − 96xy + 36y\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(4y(4x − 3)^2\)</para><para>\(2y(8x − 6)^2\)</para><para>\(4y(3x − 4)^2\)</para><para>\(4y(4x + 3)^2\) </para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \(4y(4x − 3)^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="0def5965-2187-472f-bf9b-f7864608ad0a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 6 – 10, factor using the difference of squares.</para><para>\(25v^2 − 1\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((5v − 1)(v + 5)\)</para><para>\((5v − 1)(5v + 1)\)</para><para>\((v − 5)(5v + 1)\)</para><para>\((v − 5)(v + 5)\) </para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \((5v − 1)(5v + 1)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="2fccbbb7-6910-4acd-a93e-27721115b4dd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(4 − 49x^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2 − 7x)(7 + 2x)\)</para><para>\((2 − 7x)(2 + 7x)\)</para><para>\((2 − 7x)(2 − 7x)\)</para><para>\((7 − 2x)(7 + 2x)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \((2 − 7x)(2 + 7x)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="7e7aa85d-d2e7-49eb-bb3c-fc0010d65395" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(169c^2 − 36d^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((13c − 6d)(13c + 6d)\)</para><para>\((13c + 6d)^2\)</para><para>\((13d − 6c)(13d + 6c)\)</para><para>\((13c − 6d)(13c − 6d)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.3.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \((13c − 6d)(13c + 6d)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="25eed34e-376f-4073-a444-f538099d3cd6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(121x^2 − 144y^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((12x − 11y)(12x + 11y)\)</para><para>\((12x + 11y)(12x + 11y)\)</para><para>\((11x − 12y)(11x + 12y)\)</para><para>\((11x − 12y)(11x − 12y)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.3.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \((11x − 12y)(11x + 12y)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="11cc16f4-681c-46da-b0df-1a0e480bcf21" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x^2 − 16x + 64 − y^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((x − 8 − y)^2\)</para><para> \((x + 8 − y)(x + 8 + y)\)</para><para>\((x − 8 − y)(x − 8 + y)\)</para><para>\((x − 8 − y)(x + 8 + y)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit 6.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \((x − 8 − y)(x − 8 + y)\).
      </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
